Blast radius note: state.done.probationes (check.ts:589) still demands a passed review, so no finding below lets an opus reach `done`/merge. They corrupt the board, CI signals and the append-only event log.

1. HIGH  FIFO / special-file hang stalls the whole poll (brief 143-148, 131, 155-156). Read "opens with O_NOFOLLOW, requires a regular file" - order unspecified, no O_NONBLOCK, and the 5s timeout covers git only. Probed: fs.promises.open(fifo, O_RDONLY|O_NOFOLLOW) never settles (and process.exit hung). A builder runs `mkfifo <wt>/studio/opera/W-006.md`: poll never finishes, doPoll refuses a second poll (156), board freezes at last snapshot, threadpool thread lost per FIFO.
   Fix: lstat+isFile BEFORE open; open O_RDONLY|O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK; fstat dev/ino must equal lstat's; read at most cap+1 bytes (do not trust st_size); wrap each entry in a wall-clock race (branchGitTimeoutMs). Add a mkfifo row to behaviour 5 (poll settles, committed tip served).
2. HIGH  One parseable-but-malformed live record 500s every route and the ingest (115-116, 149-150). Acceptance test is only "parseFrontMatter accepts + id equal". Probed: `probationes:\n  review: ~` makes snapshotDir throw "Cannot read properties of null (reading 'status')" (index.ts:402-405, no per-record guard). With the overlay, an UNCOMMITTED builder file takes down the Patron's board.
   Fix: at refresh, run the same per-record mapping inside try/catch (shape: state string in lifecycle STATES, probationes dict of dicts, tokens number|undefined, traditio dict); drop the entry on throw; add rows (null gate, state object, tokens string) to behaviour 5.
3. HIGH  Information-flow change not stated as one (143-148, 163-164, 525-528; D-034 ruling 2 says "live state from the branch", not "uncommitted builder edits"). The architect extended it to make `verifying` visible, then listed only half-write flicker as residual. Consequences: the builder hand-writes `state: done`, flips a human gate (hides/creates a Needs-you card), sets `tokens: 1e12` (aerarium posture, index.ts:437-445) and the Patron's board shows it, unreviewed, never through check/CI.
   Fix: say so in Intent + Residuals; live (worktree) reads may apply only when `state` is one of {building,verifying,review}; anything else (done/halted/unknown id) falls to the committed tip; ignore live `tokens` (committed tip only). Add rows.
4. MED   reviewFailedAtCertifiedTree fails OPEN (91-96, 100-103, behaviour 11 rows 380-387). "Unreadable = true" is right, but false is returned whenever the log is readable and holds no certified hash: (a) automated gates with no `certifies` (hand-deleted; probatio.certifies is advise-only, check.ts:528) - zero hashes to match; (b) log with no tree header at all; (c) certs are `dirty:H'` while the verdict header says `tree:H` for the same content; (d) the review gate's `evidence` field is hand-editable and can name any readable unrelated log (check.ts has no corroboration). Each lets `state: review` + failed review pass CI where today it blocks.
   Fix: make staleness affirmative: true unless the log parses (parseVerdictHeader `# tree:`) to a tree id AND every automated cert is `tree:` AND none equals it. Rows for (a)-(d) in behaviour 11.
5. MED   verify can be aimed at the wrong tree and write a state (66-75, 91-96; verify.ts:116,174 `--commit` -> treeHash of <ref>, pipeline index.ts:79 still runs in the repo working tree; ci.ts:150-217 `--ref` verifies a scratch checkout of any ref but writes the live studio record). `verify --commit <older-green-tree>` or `ci --ref <ref> --opus W-X` certifies a tree that is not this checkout's HEAD, probatio.certifies.stale is advise-only, and the end transition + "certified tree" predicate then write `review` for a HEAD never verified (or dodge a current failed review by naming an older tree). Also the end rule reads "every effective automated gate passed with tree:/dirty:" - a gate whose command was removed keeps an old pass (commands only built from p.command, verify.ts:~123) and counts.
   Fix: write state (start AND end) only when commit === "HEAD" and no studioRepoRelative/--ref; compute the end rule over THIS run's `results`: every effective automated id present and certifies === `${dirty?"dirty":"tree"}:${treeHash}`. Rows for --commit older, ci --ref, stale pass on commandless gate in behaviour 9.
6. MED   End write is not compare-and-set (66-75, 83). verify runs minutes; meanwhile review --fail / halt / done can run. The table says "From verifying" but not that it is tested inside editOpusFrontMatter's callback on the fresh doc (verify.ts:251 already re-parses). Decided pre-write, the end write can resurrect done/halted into review or building. Fix: CAS in the callback; if fresh state != verifying write gates only, no state, no event. Row in behaviour 9.
7. MED   Silent fail-to-trunk class (question 5). The board reverting to `greenlit` is the exact lie D-034 exists to remove. Instances: (a) 32 cap (140, behaviour 6e 323-325): for-each-ref default order is alphabetical; not stated whether the cap precedes the trunk-record filter; 32 stale/junk `opus/0*` branches hide every later in-flight opus; nothing surfaces it. (b) maxBuffer 256 KiB on for-each-ref (129): ~4k refs (trivial to create) turns the whole overlay off; stderr line repeats every 5s. (c) per-opus drops (150-154) are silent. (d) first-refresh rev-parse failure disables the overlay for the server's life with NO output (132-135) and does not distinguish "not a repo" (exit 128) from a timeout/transient. (e) clearing on any git error (138-139) makes ingest write reversal events (building->greenlit, then back) into events.jsonl; ref spam or a flapping worktree file mints unbounded permanent state_changed events (residual 2 bounds only accidental half-writes).
   Fix: --sort=-committerdate, worktree-backed branches first, count the cap AFTER the trunk filter, bound concurrency not branch count; deduped stderr line for every cap hit / per-opus drop with reason / degraded transition; keep the last good overlay for transient failures (stale-while-error) and disable for life only on "not a git repository"; larger maxBuffer; rows for each.
8. MED   CPU amplification and trunk/branch mixing (118-124, 164). snap() re-parses up to 32 x 256 KiB YAML per request on the event loop; real records are <=2 KB and store.ts:73 already caps front matter at 64 KiB. Also `opera` takes `body` from readOpusBody (store.ts:350) and `opus` reads disk via readFront - neither listed as going through the overlay though 164 promises the whole record. Fix: parse once at refresh, cache the parsed record, cap at 64 KiB; route body/opus() through the overlay entry.
9. LOW   traditio.stage relaxation (104-108). The advisory guarded a baton that disagrees with reality; active/active relaxation also silences stage AHEAD of state, e.g. handoff `review` after `review --fail` put the opus back in `building` - the misdirecting case. Fix: suppress only when rank(stage) <= rank(state) in building<verifying<review; rows for stage review/state building still advising.

Advisories:
A1. Worktree path is data from `git worktree list` (.git is builder-writable), so "realpath under worktree" is only as strong as that root. Cheap corroboration: `<wt>/.git` gitdir lies under the repo's .git/worktrees. Do the realpath check on the open fd (/proc/self/fd/N) to close the realpath->open race.
A2. BoardDrawer.tsx:59 `href={g.evidence}`: React 19.3 blocks javascript: but not data:/https phish; no CSP header anywhere in http.ts. Checked clean: no dangerouslySetInnerHTML/markdown sinks, titles escaped by React, SSE frames are one-line JSON.stringify (no frame injection).
A3. git hygiene: argv constants only; `<oid>:<studioRel>/..` cannot be read as an option and cat-file by captured object name has no TOCTOU. Scrub inherited GIT_DIR/GIT_WORK_TREE/GIT_INDEX_FILE/GIT_CONFIG*; killSignal SIGKILL; keep the overlay a Map (id "constructor" passes the id regex).
A4. verify has no actor, so anyone on the branch can flip review->verifying; accepted by the brief (88) but note it hides "awaiting review".
